# Build state never enters history: target trees carry machine paths in
# their metadata, and this repo's privacy bound is zero personal data. The
# CI privacy-firewall gate enforces the same mechanically.
target/
# The TypeScript client under web/ brings the same class of hazard in more
# forms (docs/notes/web-ui-port-inventory.md §6.3): the install tree, the
# vite build output (`out/`, not `dist/`), coverage, and the incremental
# typecheck's `tsconfig.tsbuildinfo`, which lands beside the source on the
# first local run and carries absolute paths. Widened BEFORE the first
# TypeScript file landed (the UI-1 card, §4.2).
node_modules/
web/out/
dist/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
test-results/
